  "note": "Whole-council election of the Aughnacloy Town Commissioners under the Elections and Franchise Act (Northern Ireland) 1946, polled Wednesday 18 September 1946. There was no contest: seven Unionists and two Nationalists were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 5 September 1946, p. 3). Six were re-elected (R. Sawyer, R. Elliott, W. M'Creedy, E. A. Argue, J. Brady and F. M'Vicker); the three Unionist newcomers were S. A. Henderson, J. A. Hardy and J. J. Paul. Returned unopposed."
